00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.100
Let's now take a little bit of a look at what's
going on with Corona virus.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.410
We've got four more days of data.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:12.209
The Corona virus pandemic is kind of settling
now into trends that are more about policy

00:00:12.209 --> 00:00:13.690
than early hot spots.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:20.000
And it is becoming very clear that it is overwhelmingly
red states where the case growth is explosive.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.910
Now, in the United States, in general, red
states have worse education.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:26.990
They have worse health care.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.910
They have lower incomes, they have more poverty.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.370
And these are trends that we've seen in the
United States for a long time now.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.340
Early on in Corona virus, there were many
right wingers who were almost delighting from

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:44.890
seeing hot spots in large democratic cities,
often within Democratic states.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.999
We are now more than three months in.

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:53.480
We're starting to see corona virus spread
correlate more with policy than simply where

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.750
did it go first?

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.910
And with some small exceptions, this is increasingly
a red state problem.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:05.560
Take a look at this map where you will see
a county by county growth level where either

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.619
the trends are going in the right direction
or in the wrong direction.

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:14.320
And this is a much more precise way than simply
looking at states or the country.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.340
If you're what I'll describe to you what we're
looking at.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.539
But if you're watching, you will notice there
are green and yellow colored counties.

00:01:20.539 --> 00:01:22.090
Those are doing well.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:26.990
That means they are either fully or almost
under control with corona virus.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.070
You then have orange and red counties, which
are not good.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.070
OK.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:36.060
And as you can see, huge swaths of the country,
including the northeast, most of the West

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.100
Coast other than California, which continues
to be a problem, much of the bluer states

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.060
in between are going in the right direction.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:49.400
And yet at a country level, we have crazy
numbers of new corona virus cases.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.490
How can this be?

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:54.250
Well, it's because of the really disastrous
red state counties.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.539
Almost all of Arizona is going the wrong way.

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:02.759
Large parts of Texas, Louisiana, Alabama,
Arkansas, Oklahoma, Georgia, both Carolinas,

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:03.990
Florida.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:09.479
And if you look at day to day case numbers,
the places that are now regularly having the

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:13.140
new single day case records are still California.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:18.890
We've talked about California, but then it's
places like Florida, Texas, Arizona, again,

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:24.680
the Carolinas, Georgia, couple of the early
hot spots, New York and Illinois, but then

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.680
Tennessee, Virginia, Ohio.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.560
So do we have a unifying theory about what
is going on here?

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.560
We actually do.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.849
And I'm going to tell you what it is so that
when these right wingers trot out the bogus

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:39.790
talking points, you don't fall from them to
fall for them.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.370
Some of the talking points we're hearing from
the right are things like this is a Democratic

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.909
city problem which spread.

00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:49.510
No thanks to them into red states.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:52.099
It's the fault of the Democrats.

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:56.209
We've heard red states have more cases because
they have more testing.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:03.560
We've heard this was allowed in from China
because of stupid liberal blue state governors.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.480
And now we all have a problem thanks to them.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.970
We've heard the numbers are simply fake.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.980
We've heard southern states are a problem
because Mexicans are bringing the virus across

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.540
the border.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.110
All of this is wrong.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.110
All of this is wrong.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:22.970
Trump brags that now no one is coming over
the U.S. Mexico border.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:29.549
Trump has said the border is stronger than
ever other than states lying about how low

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:31.810
they claim cases to be.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.939
The huge case numbers are not because there
is more testing going on.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:38.120
There really are more cases.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.989
This is all not true.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:43.440
And here is the unifying theory to understand.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.439
Early on, late 2019, early 2020.

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:50.950
Before we knew what was going on, before we
understood the disease and how it spread,

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:56.880
the disease was seeded planted in urban areas
with high direct traffic to the early hotspot.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.680
So here in Boston, we have tons of flights
to Europe and to China and other parts of

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.680
Asia.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:09.819
Nonstop flights here to Shanghai, Hong Kong,
Japan, multiple city, you know, Beijing, etc..

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:12.540
So it was seeded here in Boston.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.239
New York has two major airports that connect
directly to China.

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:19.959
In Europe, JFK and Newark, Pennsylvania, was
an early hotspot.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.190
American Airlines is a huge hub in Philadelphia.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.800
Huge flight hub back and forth to Europe and
even some flights to Asia.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.270
Chicago is a big hub for American Airlines
and United.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:33.400
Many international airlines also have non
stops to Chicago.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.120
You've got Los Angeles and San Francisco airport.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.500
So for two to three months, Corona virus was
being seeded before we knew what was going

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.500
on.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.140
And that's why those were the early.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.140
Hotspots.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:49.289
When we learned about what was going on and
started stay at home orders, those places

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:53.650
already had a huge amount of disease before
we even had testing capacity.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.300
It was spreading for weeks.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:05:00.810
And you had a large base population which
contributed to huge spread in these places.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:04.080
We had it here in Boston, New York, Chicago,
etc.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:10.220
So early this spread was heavily related to
where are people flying in and out of and

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.830
giving it to other people.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.460
Now, over time, some states adopted serious
policies for mitigation and some states did

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.460
not.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:23.220
And over time, the numbers became less about
flights and air travel, which have all but

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.789
stopped, but more about policy.

00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:31.830
And once you let the policy differences play
out for a few months, you see these dramatic

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:35.000
reductions in places that were early hot spots.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.350
Massachusetts, New York, Illinois, Pennsylvania,
which are crushing the disease right now.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.150
Fortunately, I'm really thrilled, by the way.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.850
But what's going on here in Massachusetts?

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:48.229
Things slowly reopening, safely reopening,
which is good to see.

00:05:48.229 --> 00:05:53.639
And you see the explosion in the places that
didn't have strict guidelines or they were

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:54.950
simply ignored.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.060
That's what's going on in California.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.060
By the way.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.610
California has strict guidelines, but from
all of the people I know living there, a lot

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.040
of people are just ignoring them.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.810
That explains California.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:09.830
It also explains Arizona, Florida, Carolinas,
Georgia, Oklahoma, Arkansas, Alabama, Louisiana

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.360
as the new growing hot spots.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.240
So policy clearly does matter.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:21.650
And at the rate things are going, if you don't
reverse what's going on right now in 15 days,

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:26.349
you are going to have a large portion of the
U.S. south that is going to be the world hot

00:06:26.349 --> 00:06:27.410
spot.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:34.210
There are states already Arizona's growth
rate for cases exceeds some of the worst countries

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.389
